  "preamble": "Fronting and unrounding of /o/ to /e/. In Latin, the sequence vo- became ve- before s, t and r plus consonant during the 2nd century BC, so that Plautine vortō, voster and vortex gave Classical vertō 'turn', vester 'your' and vertex; inherited Proto-Italic *wors-o- likewise gave verrō 'sweep'.",
